    visualBrandingNotes:
      "Modern Scandinavian-minimalist luxury in the Acne Studios / COS / Byredo lane, layered over subtle Norse motif. Cold slate-grey and oxidized iron primary, aged bronze accent, parchment-white ground, a muted oxblood reserved for active-rivalry state cues (contested-bid alerts, principal-on-site notices) and never used as ambient color, a cold pale yellow used sparingly as a signature accent echoing Odin's iris. Runic inflection lives as display typography and as trace watermark detail only — never as decorative border scrollwork, never as kitschy carved-wood Viking signage. Material feel: oiled blackened oak, brushed iron, handmade parchment, aged bronze plate. The mark should read as a serious European luxury firm that happens to be named after a mythological realm — not a guild crest, not a faction emblem, not a Marvel-adjacent comic property. Reject: horned helmets, dragon-prow silhouettes, crossed-axes-and-shield crests, illuminated-manuscript ornamentation, the Valknut symbol (real-world extremist associations), carved-wood-fantasy-tavern treatments, leather-tooled-rune sword-and-sorcery visual language, thunderbolt iconography (Thor's lane regardless), gold leaf (Golden Phoenix lane), navy-and-silver private-bank palette (Straits Meridian lane), signal-cyan (A-List Media lane).",
    leaderPortraitBrief:
      "Style: locked Ascension raster house style — modern Korean action-webtoon portrait art per docs/product/image-generation-prompting-guide.md. Crisp confident outlines, cel-adjacent shading with grouped shadow masses, restrained non-glossy highlights, muted cinematic jewel-tone palette. Tall elongated webtoon proportions. The subject is deliberately age-ambiguous and that ambiguity is the portrait's central visual joke. Subject: Odin, a man who presents as mid-70s but whose visible torso unambiguously reads as mid-40s. Face: weathered and aged — deep-set eyes, heavy brow, pronounced nasolabial lines, cool greyed complexion with visible age-spotting across the cheekbones; long wild silver-grey hair worn loose and lightly braided in places; full wild grey beard reaching the mid-chest, intentionally unkempt. Eye treatment: the left eye is covered by a well-worn aged-leather eye patch with fine rune-tooled detailing around the edge and a dark leather strap that disappears into his hair — a commissioned high-fashion piece rather than cheap costume dressing; the patch reads as an iconic Odin signature and makes the visual unmistakable at a glance. The right eye is a brilliant cold golden-yellow iris — saturated, slightly unnatural, unambiguously attunement-marked. Body: upper torso partially exposed and unmistakably younger than the face above it — sculpted mid-40s musculature across chest, shoulders, and upper abdominals, taut skin, no age-spotting below the neckline. The face-body age mismatch should read on the second look, not the first; the viewer's brain should complete the unease independently. Outfit: modern high-fashion Norse — a heavy matte-black wool cloak draped asymmetrically off one shoulder, lined with a couture-grade dark-grey long-hair fur mantle (reads as Rick Owens or Yohji Yamamoto, not as barbarian pelt); the cloak falls open across the chest to deliberately reveal the younger torso; below the waist a tailored blackened-leather wrap kilt with brushed-steel hardware and fine rune-engraved detailing; forearms wrapped in aged-bronze-and-leather rune-engraved bracers as fashion pieces, not functional gauntlets; bare feet or minimalist dark leather sandals. Prop: Gungnir — a modern ceremonial spear, held vertically in his right hand or planted beside him; matte-black hardwood shaft approximately his own height, brushed-steel head with fine rune engraving along the socket, aged-bronze binding at the collar, no bright reflective highlights. The spear reads as a commissioned high-fashion art object that is also, unambiguously, a functional weapon. Ravens: two corporeal ravens, black plumage, unmistakably real birds rather than ethereal effects, with bright golden-yellow eyes matching his remaining iris — one perched on his left shoulder with wings folded, one mid-flight behind him with wings partially spread, both rendered cleanly without motion blur. Composition: full-body standing portrait in the shipped presenter-roster canvas (~2:3, 1024x1536), slight 3/4 angle front-facing, subject centered with negative space for UI integration. Posture: still, composed, weight grounded evenly, chin slightly lifted, gaze direct on camera (single yellow eye meeting the viewer, the eye patch creating intentional asymmetry). Background: plain warm-white / off-white, no scene detail, strong silhouette separation. Reject: painterly or watercolor rendering, glossy digital highlights, horned helmets, barbarian pelts or dragon-prow styling, comic-book Thor / Viking costume language, carved-wood-fantasy-tavern aesthetics, overly gory eye treatment, age-makeup that reads as obvious prosthetics (the face should read as lived-in and plausible at first glance — the age joke lands on the torso, not on the face), over-rendered fitness-magazine abdominals (the body should read as athletic mid-40s, not as a professional physique competitor), neon glow, dark studio backgrounds, LARP Viking regalia of any kind.",
    guildInsigniaBrief:
      "Runic-inflected European-luxury mark, not a faction crest and not a fantasy emblem. Primary element: a stylized runic character — the Ansuz rune (ᚨ) rendered as a clean modernist geometric letterform in aged bronze on a parchment-white or slate-grey ground. Secondary element: a small 'ASGARD' wordmark set in a contemporary high-end serif or slab-serif with tight letterspacing, placed beneath or beside the runic mark. The runic mark must read cleanly on its own at leaderboard-row size; wordmark-tiny supplementary text is not required. Material feel: aged bronze plaque, debossed parchment stationery, blackened iron signage. The mark should look at home on a European luxury-house business card, on the facade of a design-conscious Tribeca gallery, and on a licensing-board filing, simultaneously. Reject: shield or crest silhouettes, illuminated-manuscript border ornamentation, the Valknut symbol (real-world extremist associations), crossed-axes-and-shield arrangements, horned-helmet silhouettes, dragon-prow silhouettes, thunderbolt iconography, gold leaf (Golden Phoenix lane), navy-and-silver private-bank palette (Straits Meridian lane), signal-cyan accent (A-List Media lane), generic-tech-startup geometric sans-serif, calligraphy-as-ornament, any LARP Viking visual language.",
    dossierMotif:
      "Cold slate-grey panel ground with aged-bronze border accents and a single small Ansuz runic mark in the upper-left corner. Thin aged-bronze divider line beneath the leader name. Subtle large-scale watermark behind the portrait area — a low-contrast field of elongated runic strokes with a single faintly visible raven silhouette in one quadrant — kept soft enough to read as texture rather than pattern. Muted oxblood is reserved for active-rivalry state cues (principal-on-site alert, contested-bid warning, Long Hall offer-extended notice) and is never used as ambient color. A cold pale-yellow hairline accent appears beside the leader name, echoing the yellow iris — unique to Asgard and not used as ambient color. Brand wordmark sits as a small footer in aged bronze with a slate-grey divider above it. The whole treatment should read like the lobby signage of a European luxury-brand flagship applied to a guild dossier card — quiet, expensive, and reinforcing the intentional restraint of Asgard's public identity.",
